      "username": "LonelyMan",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2025-10-27T14:32:16.020Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This episode brought to you by Monsanto.</p>\n<p>Sumac Umlaude - or perhaps just Sümac.</p>\n<p>The biggest way we know this isn’t a real thing is that nobody is like “pfft, plants are GIRLY!”  Only people who grew up thinking Wraith was the supercool bad@$$ which Batman was for us could look at a giant purple tank covered with “evil” violets and not be like “did your GIRLFRIEND send you those flowers, dorkweed?”</p>\n<p>Rebel Thorn is an OFFSHOOT?  Dude, it was right there…</p>\n<p>Ole Ander is a Swede.</p>\n<p>The Obnoxious Thicket</p>\n<p>The Cultivator should be a member that betrays the team and starts his own…sinister…quasi-religious…secretive brotherhood…of personality…</p>\n<p>Matt “Mad Dog” Mattock the Third, Esquire.  He’s a funder who obnoxiously insisted on being on the team.</p>\n<p>There’s a Swamp Thing story where his formerly human antagonist Jason Woodrue turns into a guy made of wood, who calls himself Wood-Rue and teams up with Poison Ivy to wipe out humanity.  I wonder why I thought to bring that up here.</p>",
